"phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"The LORD has sworn and will not change His mind: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”","verse":4}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Zion","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion"},"text":"The LORD extends Your mighty scepter from Zion: “Rule in the midst of Your enemies.”","verse":2}],"id":"Zion","label":"Zion","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion","term":"Zion"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Zion","sourceTitle":"Zion"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.1-7","r":"Ps.110.1-7","rawR":"Ps.110.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.1-7","value":"Ps.110.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 110"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Jesus and the apostles cite this psalm to explain Jesus’ unique ministry and status as the Messiah (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.22.43-45","r":"Matt.22.43-45","rawR":"Matt.22.43-45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.22.43-45","value":"Matt.22.43-45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 22:43-45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.32-36","r":"Acts.2.32-36","rawR":"Acts.2.32-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.32-36","value":"Acts.2.32-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:32-36"},"). It reaffirms God’s covenant with David and gives hope for the future (see ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.7.8-16","r":"2Sam.7.8-16","rawR":"2Sam.7.8-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.7.8-16","value":"2Sam.7.8-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sam 7:8-16"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.1-7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.1-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"827b5da99f914bcd8cfc0484d5d7066289e625c4480eefd2b74fe671dcefacde","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.1-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7169,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.1-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.1-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.1","r":"Ps.110.1","rawR":"Ps.110.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.1","value":"Ps.110.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The king of Israel had the great privilege of being the Lord’s adopted son (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.22.10","r":"1Chr.22.10","rawR":"1Chr.22.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.22.10","value":"1Chr.22.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 22:10"},"), but he fell (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.1-52","r":"Ps.89.1-52","rawR":"Ps.89.1-52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.1-52","value":"Ps.89.1-52"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 89"},"). This decree restores and heightens his position. • ",{"c":["The"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":[":"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Hebrew ",{"c":["Yahweh,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," the name of God (see ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.3.6-14","r":"Exod.3.6-14","rawR":"Exod.3.6-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.3.6-14","value":"Exod.3.6-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 3:6-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.2-8","r":"Exod.6.2-8","rawR":"Exod.6.2-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.2-8","value":"Exod.6.2-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:2-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.20.2","r":"Exod.20.2","rawR":"Exod.20.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.20.2","value":"Exod.20.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:2"},"). • ",{"c":["my Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["’adoni"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") means “my master” or “my superior.” The psalmist viewed God’s messianic ruler as his superior. The New Testament frequently cites this psalm to validate Jesus’ claim to be the Messiah (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.22.44-45","r":"Matt.22.44-45","rawR":"Matt.22.44-45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.22.44-45","value":"Matt.22.44-45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 22:44-45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.12.36-37","r":"Mark.12.36-37","rawR":"Mark.12.36-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.12.36-37","value":"Mark.12.36-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 12:36-37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.20.42-44","r":"Luke.20.42-44","rawR":"Luke.20.42-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.20.42-44","value":"Luke.20.42-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 20:42-44"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.34-35","r":"Acts.2.34-35","rawR":"Acts.2.34-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.34-35","value":"Acts.2.34-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:34-35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.1.13","r":"Heb.1.13","rawR":"Heb.1.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.1.13","value":"Heb.1.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 1:13"},"). • The Lord’s ",{"c":["right hand"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," represents his authority, strength, presence, and benefits. The Lord chose the descendant of David and raised him up to be close to him (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.80.17","r":"Ps.80.17","rawR":"Ps.80.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.80.17","value":"Ps.80.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 80:17"},"). Jesus claimed this position for himself (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.26.64","r":"Matt.26.64","rawR":"Matt.26.64","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.26.64","value":"Matt.26.64"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 26:64"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.14.62","r":"Mark.14.62","rawR":"Mark.14.62","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.14.62","value":"Mark.14.62"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 14:62"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.16.19","r":"Mark.16.19","rawR":"Mark.16.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.16.19","value":"Mark.16.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.22.69","r":"Luke.22.69","rawR":"Luke.22.69","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.22.69","value":"Luke.22.69"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 22:69"},"), and the apostles announced that Jesus, having ascended to heaven, sits at the right hand of the Father (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.33","r":"Acts.2.33","rawR":"Acts.2.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.33","value":"Acts.2.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.5.31","r":"Acts.5.31","rawR":"Acts.5.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.5.31","value":"Acts.5.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.7.55-56","r":"Acts.7.55-56","rawR":"Acts.7.55-56","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.7.55-56","value":"Acts.7.55-56"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:55-56"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.8.34","r":"Rom.8.34","rawR":"Rom.8.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.8.34","value":"Rom.8.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 8:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.1.20","r":"Eph.1.20","rawR":"Eph.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.1.20","value":"Eph.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 1:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.3.1","r":"Col.3.1","rawR":"Col.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.3.1","value":"Col.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 3:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.1.3","r":"Heb.1.3","rawR":"Heb.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.1.3","value":"Heb.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 1:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.8.1","r":"Heb.8.1","rawR":"Heb.8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.8.1","value":"Heb.8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.12","r":"Heb.10.12","rawR":"Heb.10.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.12","value":"Heb.10.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.12.2","r":"Heb.12.2","rawR":"Heb.12.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.12.2","value":"Heb.12.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:2"},"). • Ancient Near Eastern kings were sometimes portrayed as placing their feet on the backs of their conquered ",{"c":["enemies"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," as on a ",{"c":["footstool"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (see ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.12-13","r":"Heb.10.12-13","rawR":"Heb.10.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.12-13","value":"Heb.10.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 10:12-13"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.1","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c3b0ff0cf106ef373963c0101ea73088dfb822970f27a258d91ca7fd9e24adfa","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7170,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.2-3","r":"Ps.110.2-3","rawR":"Ps.110.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.2-3","value":"Ps.110.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:2-3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["kingdom"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," will expand and increase, beginning from Jerusalem, until all enemies are conquered."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.2-3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.2-3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dbf3f5df7c829186cc0a6ceb73ffc1289c65224551d380901ef1e5364608510f","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.2-3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7171,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.2-3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.2-3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.4","r":"Ps.110.4","rawR":"Ps.110.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.4","value":"Ps.110.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The Lord had made an unbreakable ",{"c":["oath"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and covenant, so his apparent rejection of David’s dynasty (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.38","r":"Ps.89.38","rawR":"Ps.89.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.38","value":"Ps.89.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"89:38"},") in the Exile had led to a crisis. The placement of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.1-7","r":"Ps.110.1-7","rawR":"Ps.110.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.1-7","value":"Ps.110.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 110"}," in Book Five reaffirms the future of the dynasty: David’s descendant must conform to God’s standard of integrity (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.101.1-8","r":"Ps.101.1-8","rawR":"Ps.101.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.101.1-8","value":"Ps.101.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 101"},"). His ministry will be transformed as he serves under God’s kingship (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.93.1-100.5","r":"Ps.93.1-100.5","rawR":"Ps.93.1-100.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.93.1-100.5","value":"Ps.93.1-100.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 93–100"},"). • ",{"c":["You are a priest forever:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The role of God’s messianic ruler changes. The priestly kingship of David and his descendants extended to serving as patrons of the Temple. David had the Ark brought to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.6.15","r":"2Sam.6.15","rawR":"2Sam.6.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.6.15","value":"2Sam.6.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sam 6:15"},") and arranged for the Temple service (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.31-48","r":"1Chr.6.31-48","rawR":"1Chr.6.31-48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.31-48","value":"1Chr.6.31-48"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:31-48"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.11-26","r":"1Chr.15.11-26","rawR":"1Chr.15.11-26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.11-26","value":"1Chr.15.11-26"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:11-26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.4-42","r":"1Chr.16.4-42","rawR":"1Chr.16.4-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.4-42","value":"1Chr.16.4-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:4-42"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.4-32","r":"1Chr.23.4-32","rawR":"1Chr.23.4-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.4-32","value":"1Chr.23.4-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:4-32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1","r":"1Chr.25.1","rawR":"1Chr.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1","value":"1Chr.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1"},"). Solomon supervised the Temple construction (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.5.1-7.51","r":"1Kgs.5.1-7.51","rawR":"1Kgs.5.1-7.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.5.1-7.51","value":"1Kgs.5.1-7.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 5:1–7:51"},"). Even so, Israel’s kingship was separate from its priesthood. In the messianic kingdom, the king would also minister as priest, as ",{"c":["Melchizedek"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," king of Salem (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.18","r":"Gen.14.18","rawR":"Gen.14.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.18","value":"Gen.14.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 14:18"},"), had done. The New Testament develops the ministry of Jesus Christ as a fulfillment of this new order (see ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.5.6-10","r":"Heb.5.6-10","rawR":"Heb.5.6-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.5.6-10","value":"Heb.5.6-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 5:6-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.6.20-7.25","r":"Heb.6.20-7.25","rawR":"Heb.6.20-7.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.6.20-7.25","value":"Heb.6.20-7.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:20–7:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"bbbc6d77fbf27090f7b93119431548457f62cf9d2156983640e87740eb9cb425","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7172,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.5-7","r":"Ps.110.5-7","rawR":"Ps.110.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.5-7","value":"Ps.110.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:5-7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The new priestly role of David’s descendant does not rescind his old role as conquering ruler. He must still bring the nations under his rule (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.2-3","r":"Ps.110.2-3","rawR":"Ps.110.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.2-3","value":"Ps.110.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:2-3"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.5-7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.5-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"11a295d902e6e6d0ce6f8520c365f4affa4eb8782a3afb2cf4e4524ae196d696","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.5-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7173,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.5-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.5-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.5-6","r":"Ps.110.5-6","rawR":"Ps.110.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.5-6","value":"Ps.110.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:5-6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["at your right hand:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This position brings help and protection (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.7-8","r":"Ps.16.7-8","rawR":"Ps.16.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.7-8","value":"Ps.16.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:7-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.108.13","r":"Ps.108.13","rawR":"Ps.108.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.108.13","value":"Ps.108.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"108:13"},"). • The Lord ",{"c":["will strike down"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," rebellious ",{"c":["kings"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". Rebellion against the Lord is a capital offense (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.6.23","r":"Rom.6.23","rawR":"Rom.6.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.6.23","value":"Rom.6.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 6:23"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.5-6","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.5-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"685450a1734e19f2fbdbbc1966d95a696a089fdcea561717fb5173568073b5ef","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.5-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7174,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.5-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.5-6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.7","r":"Ps.110.7","rawR":"Ps.110.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.7","value":"Ps.110.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," God’s messianic ruler obtains victory as a vigorous person, as if he had received nourishment ",{"c":["from brooks along the way"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.3","r":"Ps.110.3","rawR":"Ps.110.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.3","value":"Ps.110.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.110.7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":110,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":110,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.110.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[110],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ef47f75cdf9fbf0b2fc9109700db6fcc3f51a3fde2a755e72493950340357f46","sourceItemName":"Ps.110.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7175,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.110.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.110.7","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}